abstract: >-
  Code, synthetic input data, and results for a simulation-based economic
  evaluation of information system reliability. The system is represented by
  five mutually exclusive states with an admissible transition matrix and a
  transition probability matrix per architecture; economic losses are
  accumulated along simulated hourly system state trajectories using state-specific
  cost rates scaled by a time-dependent business criticality coefficient. The
  repository reproduces the estimated expected economic losses, loss quantiles,
  generalized multi-state availability, empirical exceedance frequencies, net economic
  benefit, the choice of the number of simulation runs, and the sensitivity
  analysis and Figs. 2-4 of the article. All parameters are synthetic and
  expressed in illustrative monetary units.
